summary:
FAIL on one new Medium finding; all three of my round-5 findings are closed.

F-DG6-360, F-DG6-361 and F-DG6-362 verify CLOSED_VERIFIED on candidate 0fea8adf:
- the round-5 reproductions no longer reproduce;
- a wider probe covers a sensitive business case, a second benefit and a sensitive evidence item, across 238 drill-down variants with every page followed, every live report and subject, and the dashboards;
- mutants that revert each fix are caught by the repaired sweep and the new tests.

The F-DG6-340 and F-DG6-380 repairs are also shown to be caught by their tests (mutants M3 and M4). BE-Z8 is sound. The BE-Z7B residuals are acceptable.

Required runs:
- the full integration suite passes twice (LANG unset and C.UTF-8: 424 files, 4253 passed, 1 skipped, 1 todo, contract 932 of 932);
- the static checks and the build pass;
- the historical DG1-DG5 validations pass;
- 38/38 security-relevant root e2e tests pass;
- pnpm test passes every test on Node 22 and 24, but exits 1 on a load-induced Vitest RPC timeout that disappears with 2 workers.

New: F-DG6-420 (Medium, not mandatory, REQ-S10-002). Benefit groups name a restricted benefit's id (countedBenefitId, memberBenefitIds), and an open measurement's evidenceIds names a sensitive evidence item, to a reader who gets 404 on both. ADR-0051 §2 says existence is not disclosed and does not decide references. Medium findings must be repaired or decided before the gate (D-192), so the verdict is FAIL.
